# Line-ending policy.
#
# This repo had neither .gitattributes nor core.autocrlf, so a Windows checkout
# rewrote every line of every text file and `git status` reported whole files as
# modified when nothing had changed — 2,391 phantom insertions and 2,391 phantom
# deletions across three files. That is not cosmetic: it buries the real diff,
# makes review meaningless, and risks committing a stale data snapshot over a
# newer one because the file "looks changed anyway".
#
# Normalise to LF in the repository; Git still checks out native endings where
# the platform wants them.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Committed API snapshots are content-hashed for change detection. Pin them to
# LF so a line-ending rewrite can never masquerade as new data.
data/*.json  text eol=lf

# Windows batch files genuinely need CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
